x":"To find the sum of all multiples of 7 between 100 and 200, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the smallest and largest multiples of 7 in the given range:**\n   - The smallest multiple of 7 greater than or equal to 100 can be found by dividing 100 by 7 and rounding up to the nearest whole number.\n     \\[\n     \\frac{100}{7} \\approx 14.2857 \\implies \\lceil 14.2857 \\rceil = 15\n     \\]\n     So, the smallest multiple of 7 is \\( 7 \\times 15 = 105 \\).\n\n   - The largest multiple of 7 less than or equal to 200 can be found by dividing 200 by 7 and rounding down to the nearest whole number.\n     \\[\n     \\frac{200}{7} \\approx 28.5714 \\implies \\lfloor 28.5714 \\rfloor = 28\n     \\]\n     So, the largest multiple of 7 is \\( 7 \\times 28 = 196 \\).\n\n2. **List the multiples of 7 between 100 and 200:**\n   The multiples of 7 between 105 and 196 are:\n   \\[\n   105, 112, 119, \\ldots, 196\n   \\]\n   This is an arithmetic sequence where the first term \\( a = 105 \\) and the common difference \\( d = 7 \\).\n\n","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,3838,374,279,2629,315,678,315,279,65060,315,220,22,1948,220,16,15,15,323,220,17,15,15,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198,1249,1477,279,2629,315,678,65060,315,220,22,1948,220,16,15,15,323,220,17,15,15,11,582,646,1795,1493,7354,1447,16,13,3070,28301,1437,279,24632,323,7772,65060,315,220,22,304,279,2661,2088,25,1019,256,481,576,24632,5248,315,220,22,7046,1091,476,6144,311,220,16,15,15,646,387,1730,553,49702,220,16,15,15,553,220,22,323,51562,705,311,279,23480,4361,1372,624,257,1124,9640,257,1124,37018,90,16,15,15,15170,22,92,1124,48053,220,16,19,13,17,23,20,22,1124,6383,550,1124,75,22058,220,16,19,13,17,23,20,22,1124,81,22058,284,220,16,20,198,257,1124,921,257,2055,11,279,24632,5248,315,220,22,374,17767,220,22,1124,15136,220,16,20,28