\\times (105 + 196) = 7 \\times 301 = 2107\n   \\]\n\nThus, the sum of all multiples of 7 between 100 and 200 is \\(\\boxed{2107}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2107}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To find the sum of all multiples of 7 between 100 and 200, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the smallest and largest multiples of 7 in the given range:**\n   - The smallest multiple of 7 greater than or equal to 100 can be found by dividing 100 by 7 and rounding up to the nearest whole number.\n     \\[\n     \\frac{100}{7} \\approx 14.2857 \\implies \\lceil 14.2857 \\rceil = 15\n     \\]\n     So, the smallest multiple of 7 is \\( 7 \\times 15 = 105 \\).\n\n   - The largest multiple of 7 less than or equal to 200 can be found by dividing 200 by 7 and rounding down to the nearest whole number.\n     \\[\n     \\frac{200}{7} \\approx 28.5714 \\implies \\lfloor 28.5714 \\rfloor = 28\n     \\]\n     So, the largest multiple of 7 is \\( 7 \\times 28 = 196 \\).\n\n2. **List the multiples of 7 between 100 and 200:**\n   The multiples of 7 between 105 and 196 are:\n   \\[\n   105, 112, 119, \\ldots, 196\n   \\]\n   This is an arithmetic sequence where the first term \\( a = 105 \\) and the common difference \\( d = 7 \\).\n\n3. **Find the number of terms in this sequence:**\n   The general form of the \\( n \\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n   \\[\n   a_n = a + (n-1)d\n   \\]\n   Setting \\( a_n = 196 \\):\n   \\[\n   196 = 105 + (n-1) \\cdot 7\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( n \\):\n   \\[\n   196 - 105 = (n-1) \\cdot 7 \\implies 91 = (n-1) \\cdot 7 \\implies n-1 = \\frac{91}{7} = 13 \\implies n = 14\n   \\]\n   Thus, there are 14 terms in this sequence.\n\n4. **Calculate the sum of the arithmetic sequence:**\n   The sum \\( S_n \\) of the first \\( n \\) terms of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n   \\[\n   S_n = \\frac{n}{2} \\times (a + l)\n   \\]\n   where \\( l \\) is the last term. Here, \\( n = 14 \\), \\( a = 105 \\), and \\( l = 196 \\):\n   \\[\n   S_{14} = \\frac{14}{2} \\times (105 + 196) = 7 \\times 301 = 2107\n   \\]\n\nThus, the sum of all multiples of 7 between 100 and 200 is \\(\\boxed{2107}\\).","id":"algebra:748"}
